They have five key principles.

00:57:55.760 --> 00:57:59.088
Principle number one, they're universally accessible.

00:57:59.264 --> 00:58:02.986
Try to get these in a way that every kid can do it, or as many kids as possible.

00:58:03.088 --> 00:58:06.198
Number two, they're developmentally appropriate for the kid.

00:58:06.294 --> 00:58:10.010
They emphasize motor skills and foundational human movement.

00:58:10.350 --> 00:58:12.010
Again, you may be surprised.

00:58:12.350 --> 00:58:16.278
There's no maximum cleaning jerks here. There's no vertical jump.

00:58:16.454 --> 00:58:19.650
This is the stuff that athletic development model should be after.

00:58:20.270 --> 00:58:22.918
Number three, it is multi sport participation.

00:58:23.094 --> 00:58:29.770
You'll be surprised to learn even the Olympic Committee here wants kids to play multiple sports.

00:58:30.070 --> 00:58:32.330
They do not want you to specialize early.

00:58:32.630 --> 00:58:34.526
