And this is just what I'm calling additional resources. I promised this earlier.

01:41:55.576 --> 01:41:57.200
There are a handful of books that I know.

01:41:57.240 --> 01:42:03.046
I have personally read certifications and courses that I thought were great and I wanted to directly mention those.

01:42:03.118 --> 01:42:05.318
More again will be available in the show notes.

01:42:05.414 --> 01:42:11.446
But from a textbook perspective, the NSCA's High School Strength and conditioning book is fantastic.

01:42:11.478 --> 01:42:17.126
If your kid is at that age, you want to know direct exercise examples, programs, how to teach

01:42:17.158 --> 01:42:22.166
the exercises, the techniques, all that stuff. It's wonderful. Patrick McHenry.

01:42:22.198 --> 01:42:23.926
I've known Patrick for a long time. Mike Nitkin.

01:42:23.958 --> 01:42:27.742
Mike is just a legendary figure in youth strength training.

